AJALI! — ADMIN OPERATIONS PANEL

We are currently building ONLY the ADMIN SIDE of Ajali!.

Do not redesign, rebuild, or modify the public citizen-facing pages unless an existing shared component must be updated.

The goal is to build a complete, enterprise-style Admin Operations Panel for receiving, reviewing, tracking, moderating, updating, and resolving emergency incident reports.

CURRENT STACK:
- React
- Vite
- TypeScript / TSX
- Tailwind CSS
- shadcn/ui
- Redux Toolkit
- React Router
- api.ts as the mock API/service layer
- PWA
- Figma as the visual source of truth

We are in Sprint 1, so there is NO Flask backend yet.

==================================================
1. CORE ARCHITECTURE
==================================================

Treat api.ts as a temporary REST API abstraction.

The Admin UI must NEVER directly manipulate seed/mock data.

Use:

Admin UI
↓
Redux / hooks
↓
API service layer
↓
Mock implementation in api.ts

Later:

Admin UI
↓
Redux / hooks
↓
API service layer
↓
Flask REST API
↓
PostgreSQL

The Admin UI should not need to be rewritten when the mock API is replaced by Flask.

Do not create demo-only logic inside React components.

