7. INCIDENT REVIEW / MODERATION
==================================================

Route:

/admin/incidents/:id/review

This is the main moderation workspace.

The admin should be able to review:

- Incident details
- Reporter
- Location
- Evidence
- Severity
- Existing notes
- Status history

Actions depend on the current status.

PENDING:

[Verify]
[Close as False/Invalid]
[Edit]

VERIFIED:

[Start Response]
[Close]
[Edit]

IN_PROGRESS:

[Resolve]
[Update Severity]
[Add Note]

RESOLVED:

[View History]
[Reopen if allowed]

CLOSED:

[View History]
[Reopen if allowed]

Do not allow invalid lifecycle transitions.

Sensitive actions should require a confirmation dialog and reason.

==================================================
8. INCIDENT LIFECYCLE
==================================================

Use these statuses:

PENDING
VERIFIED
IN_PROGRESS
RESOLVED
CLOSED

Normal flow:

PENDING
→ VERIFIED
→ IN_PROGRESS
→ RESOLVED

False/invalid flow:

PENDING
→ CLOSED

Rules:

PENDING:
Received but not yet verified.

VERIFIED:
Admin has confirmed the report is legitimate.

IN_PROGRESS:
Emergency response is active.

RESOLVED:
Incident has been handled.

CLOSED:
False, invalid, duplicate, or otherwise closed report.

IMPORTANT:

Only IN_PROGRESS incidents appear on the public active map.

Every status change must create:

- Status history record
- Audit log record
- Notification event

