15. MOCK API / SERVICE LAYER
==================================================

Do not let pages access mock arrays directly.

Create service functions such as:

incidentApi.getAll()
incidentApi.getById(id)
incidentApi.create(data)
incidentApi.update(id, data)
incidentApi.archive(id, reason)

incidentApi.verify(id, reason)
incidentApi.close(id, reason)
incidentApi.startResponse(id, reason)
incidentApi.resolve(id, reason)
incidentApi.reopen(id, reason)

incidentApi.getHistory(id)
incidentApi.addNote(id, note)

adminApi.getDashboardStats()
adminApi.getAuditLogs()

notificationApi.getAll()
notificationApi.markAsRead(id)

mediaApi.add()
mediaApi.remove()

Use strongly typed request/response interfaces.

The exact names can follow the existing project conventions.

==================================================
16. STATEFUL MOCK BEHAVIOUR
==================================================

The mock API must behave like a real backend.

Example:

Admin verifies:

PENDING
→ VERIFIED

Then immediately:

- Incident list updates
- Detail page updates
- Dashboard counts update
- Status timeline updates
- Audit log updates
- Notification event is created

Admin starts response:

VERIFIED
→ IN_PROGRESS

Then:

- Public active map data includes the incident
- Dashboard updates
- Audit log updates
- Notification event is generated

Admin resolves:

IN_PROGRESS
→ RESOLVED

Then:

- Incident disappears from active incident dataset
- Dashboard updates
- History updates
- Audit log updates
- Notification event is generated

Do not fake these changes at the component level.

